{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Its blood is in its soul.</b> Meaning — in the place of its soul. And by this He gives a reason why one must cover its blood, for since its blood is its soul, it is part of proper conduct to treat it with honor, just as HaShem commanded to bury a dead person on account of his honor." "And the reason He did not say as He said regarding the animal, ״נַפְשׁוֹ בְּדָמוֹ״ — perhaps it is because the animal does possess a soul, and it is placed in the blood, but wild beast and bird do not have a soul like the animal; rather, the blood is in the place of the soul. And on this basis they do not come upon the altar to atone like the animal, except for turtledoves and young pigeons, and even they do not have their blood sprinkled on the altar but only applied by pinching (מולק)." "<b>For the soul of all flesh, etc.</b> Meaning, it is not because the blood atones on the altar that I have forbidden the blood — for then you would distinguish between the blood of an animal and the blood of wild beast and bird; rather, the reason for the prohibition is because of ״כִּי נֶפֶשׁ כָּל בָּשָׂר״ and so forth, and from this it follows that wild beast and bird are included as well." "<b>All who eat of it shall be cut off.</b> I have already written above the reason for excision (כָּרֵת). And the reason He said ״אֹכְלָיו״ in the plural and ״יִכָּרֵת״ in the singular, is to draw your attention to our interpretation: that excision means the life-force (חִיּוּנִיּוּת) that illuminates the root of his soul is withdrawn and that root is cut off — therefore He used the singular. And He said ״אֹכְלָיו״ in the plural, because those who derive benefit from the eating are many, for the life-force that is bound to the supernal root has beneath it preparatory levels so that it can subsist together with the body — for the body is physical matter, and HaShem created within it a motive force, which is the soul (nefesh), whose disposition inclines toward the physical and lusts after its pleasures; and HaShem blessed be He created them with this disposition so that it might blend with the body. And it is prepared for the level of being equated (נִשְׁתַּוֶּה) to the ruach, and the ruach is prepared for the neshamah, and the neshamah is prepared for the indwelling of His Shekhinah upon those who are worthy. From this it follows that when a person eats blood, behold there are before you multiple eaters: the body, the nefesh, the ruach, and the neshamah. And regarding the aspect of the punishment, which is excision, nothing is cut off except the thread of the neshamah that is connected above, and by this all the branches wither — therefore He used the plural." "<b>Further,</b> he wished, according to what they said of blessed memory (Torat Kohanim 17:10), that the congregation is not subject to excision for the sin of eating blood — therefore He said ״אֹכְלָיו״ in the plural and ״יִכָּרֵת״ in the singular, to say that even if many eat, excision applies only to the individual and not to the congregation." "<b>And I set it upon my heart</b> to know what reason HaShem would command to cover the blood of a wild animal (חַיָּה) and of a bird but not the blood of a domestic animal (בְּהֵמָה). Granted, blood sprinkled upon the altar — splendor and glory to it from the blood of a wild animal and bird; but blood of secular slaughter (שְׁחִיטַת חֻלִּין) that falls and is exposed to the eyes — why should a domestic animal be diminished compared to a wild animal? And all the more so given that we find that Kah chose for Himself a sacrifice from the domestic animal and not from the wild animal or bird, aside from turtledoves and young pigeons." "Now, according to what we have explained — that a wild animal's blood is the soul (נֶפֶשׁ) itself, which is not so for the domestic animal, for it has a soul apart from the blood and it is compounded in the blood, yet its blood itself is not its soul — therefore HaShem did not command to cover any blood except that blood which is itself the soul, unlike the domestic animal, whose blood itself is not the soul as is the case with the wild animal and the bird. And even though there is soul in the blood of a domestic animal as well, nevertheless the blood itself is not the soul, and covering applies only to what is perceptible (מוּרְגָּשׁ) and not to the hylé (הִיּוּלִי) — though it is present — and understand this." "And it seemed to me to set the mind to understand why the creation of a wild animal differs from that of a domestic animal in this regard. And it appears that the reason is according to what has preceded us in our contemplation of the intelligible flow of the effluences of existence and the sustaining of every being — for El the Creator, blessed be He, is the life-force of all, and He prepared and made conduits so that every existent would receive its supply of what it needs for its continued existence. And He divided all His creations into four levels, and they are fire, air (רוּחַ), water, and earth, and each one contains all four. And these four, the beginning of their coming-into-being is hidden from the eyes of all flesh, and it is spiritual in the utmost degree of spirituality, and they are the four legs of the throne of His glory, blessed be He. And from them flow, in kind, four other creations — the bearers of the throne: the face of a man, the face of an eagle, the face of a lion, the face of an ox — and corresponding to them, four angels: Gavriel, Refael, Michael, Nuriel; these prepare for those and receive this from that. And parallel to them, below, there are recipients among living creatures: man, ox, eagle, lion — man: the human species; ox: the domestic animal species; lion: the wild animal species; eagle: the bird species. And corresponding to them among the inanimate (דּוֹמְמִים): earth, water, fire, air — and each one contains all four. And also in the aspect of the souls, which are the supreme creation among supremacies that HaShem created from supernal lights — the portion of HaShem blessed be He — so too aspects will be found, and the rule returns that each bearer and bearer includes all of this, and each level flows forth and receives from the level of the throne of glory, which is above the holy creatures (חַיּוֹת הַקֹּדֶשׁ), down to the level of the inanimate (דּוֹמֵם)." "And now I shall come to examine the recipients that are patterned after the four revealed aspects — their likeness being above — and behold, there is the aspect of the ox, a pure domestic animal, that receives from the likeness of the face of the ox. But a wild animal and a bird — we do not find among the patterned ones (הַנִּדְמִים) [creatures] receiving below from those that receive from holiness, for the lion is an impure wild animal, and the eagle is an impure bird. And one must investigate this: why was the patterned form prevented from receiving the aspect of holiness and purity as the ox received? Moreover, from where was the aspect of purity drawn for the other pure wild animals that the Torah permitted — ״אַיָּל וּצְבִי״ and so forth?" "Know that there are levels where the recipient has no capacity to receive in the intensity of the bestower in their aspect — in the secret of the reason עוֹנִי חַכְמֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, as is known to those who know understanding, in the contemplation that is correct in discerning intellect. And therefore, because the lion and the eagle below came in intensity, they could not bear the measure given and apportioned to them in the disposition of their quality. And on account of the deficiency in their reception of the effusion of supply from the aspect of the fountain (הַנִּרְזָב) that is in the Garden of HaShem — commensurate with the measure of success reaching them from the channel directed toward them — this is a reason for their distance, which HaShem commanded a man of Israel not to draw near to them. For a man of Israel succeeded in the channel toward him in the secret of His saying (Deuteronomy 4:4) ״הַדְּבֵקִים בַה׳״, and the measure that reached the aspect of lion and eagle — its like and its measure branched off into some of the wild animals and birds, and He established in them a measure of supply. And even though their quality came only by way of nesher (eagle), for the first recipient — this is the secret of (Job 14:4) ״מִי יִתֵּן טָהוֹר מִטָּמֵא״ etc. And all this the Blessed One did for a known reason — the secret of HaShem to those who fear Him. And since this is so, the disposition of the holiness and purity that extends through the aspect of the domestic animal is not like the aspect of the wild animal and the bird, for the aspect of the ox has a counterpart above it, in the source of holiness that the Creator created and in which He established the soul — which is not so for the aspect of the wild animal and the bird. Because the likeness of the patterned form to the bestower was severed, behold it is impure before us, as it is written (Leviticus 11:13) ״אֶת הַנֶּשֶׁר וְאֶת״ etc. ״תְּשַׁקְּצוּ״ — its power is exhausted and there remains in it only the vital force (הַחִיּוּנִיּוּת), which is pure blood, as He said ״דָּמוֹ בְנַפְשׁוֹ״, and as he explained: its blood in place of its soul. Aside from turtledoves and young pigeons, which El Elyon knows that the vital force overcame in them and they are blended between the domestic animal and the bird — for from them one brings a burnt offering and a sin-offering specifically, and for an individual specifically and not for the community — and they require covering, for they have not reached the category of the domestic animal. All this I have written, if HaShem wills, and the discerning one will discern the word of the living Elohim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {9 "The phrase סוֹד טַעַם עוֹנִי חַכְמֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל appears to reference a kabbalistic doctrine known from later sources; the phrase is translated literally without expanding on its precise intent. The word הַנִּרְזָב (rendered 'fountain') is a rare term, possibly from Judaeo-Arabic; the translation reflects the contextual sense of a supernal source of flow."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:58:43.070589554Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}